    "final_answer": "I have successfully completed the task. Let me provide a clear summary of what was accomplished.\n\n## Task Completion Summary\n\n### Step 1: Found a Parking Lot in Gloucester\nI searched for \"parking lot in Gloucester MA\" and selected **City Lot**:\n- **Name**: City Lot\n- **Address**: 102 Rogers St, Gloucester, MA 01930, USA\n- **Category**: Parking lot (wheelchair accessible)\n- **Rating**: 4.3 stars (4 reviews)\n\n### Step 2: Set Up Route (Ride) to North Plymouth\nI clicked the Directions (路线) button, swapped origin/destination, and set:\n- **Starting point**: City Lot, Gloucester, MA (USA)\n- **Destination**: North Plymouth, Plymouth, Massachusetts (USA)\n\n### Step 3: Viewed the Map Route\nThe map clearly shows three driving route options from City Lot (north shore of Massachusetts) south through Boston to North Plymouth:\n\n| Route | Duration | Distance | Highway |\n|-------|----------|----------|---------|\n| **Best (Fastest)** | 1 hour 30 min | 73.7 miles | MA-128 S and MA-3 S (has tolls) |\n| Alternative | 1 hour 32 min | 77.7 miles | I-93 S and MA-3 S |\n| Alternative | 1 hour 43 min | 91.7 miles | I-95 S and MA-3 S |\n\n### Important Note About \"Booking a Ride\"\nGoogle Maps in this version does **not** display a ridesharing/打车 (Uber/Lyft) booking option in the directions panel — only driving, public transit, walking, and cycling options are available. The route has been successfully planned with the fastest driving route highlighted on the map (shown in dark blue, traveling south from Gloucester through Beverly/Salem, around Boston, and down to North Plymouth via the South Shore). To actually book a rideshare, a separate Uber/Lyft app would be required.",
